8	NAME
9	====
10	
11	eza — a modern replacement for ls
12	
13	
14	SYNOPSIS
15	========
16	
17	`eza [options] [files...]`
18	
19	**eza** is a modern replacement for `ls`.
20	It uses colours for information by default, helping you distinguish between many types of files, such as whether you are the owner, or in the owning group.
21	
22	It also has extra features not present in the original `ls`, such as viewing the Git status for a directory, or recursing into directories with a tree view.
23	
24	
25	EXAMPLES
26	========
27	
28	`eza`
29	: Lists the contents of the current directory in a grid.
30	
31	`eza --oneline --reverse --sort=size`
32	: Displays a list of files with the largest at the top.
33	
34	`eza --long --header --inode --git`
35	: Displays a table of files with a header, showing each file’s metadata, inode, and Git status.
36	
37	`eza --long --tree --level=3`
38	: Displays a tree of files, three levels deep, as well as each file’s metadata.
39	
40	
41	META OPTIONS
42	===============
43	
44	`--help`
45	: Show list of command-line options.
46	
47	`-v`, `--version`
48	: Show version of eza.
49	
50	DISPLAY OPTIONS
51	===============
52	
53	`-1`, `--oneline`
54	: Display one entry per line.
55	
56	`--absolute=WHEN`
57	: Display entries with their absolute path.
58	
59	Valid settings are '`on`', '`follow`', and '`off`'.
60	When used without a value, defaults to '`on`'.
61	
62	'`on`': Show absolute paths for all entries.
63	'`follow`': Show absolute paths and resolve symbolic links to their targets.
64	'`off`': Show relative paths (default behavior).
65	
66	`-F`, `--classify=WHEN`
67	: Display file kind indicators next to file names.
68	
69	Valid settings are ‘`always`’, ‘`automatic`’ (or ‘`auto`’ for short), and ‘`never`’.
70	When used without a value, defaults to ‘`automatic`’.
71	
72	`automatic` or `auto` will display file kind indicators only when the standard output is connected to a real terminal. If `eza` is ran while in a `tty`, or the output of `eza` is either redirected to a file or piped into another program, file kind indicators will not be used. Setting this option to ‘`always`’ causes `eza` to always display file kind indicators, while ‘`never`’ disables the use of file kind indicators.
73	
74	`-G`, `--grid`
75	: Display entries as a grid (default).
76	
77	`-l`, `--long`
78	: Display extended file metadata as a table.
79	
80	`-R`, `--recurse`
81	: Recurse into directories.
82	
83	`-T`, `--tree`
84	: Recurse into directories as a tree.
85	
86	`--follow-symlinks`
87	: Drill down into symbolic links that point to directories.
88	
89	`-X`, `--dereference`
90	: Dereference symbolic links when displaying information.
91	
92	`-x`, `--across`
93	: Sort the grid across, rather than downwards.
94	
95	`--color=WHEN`, `--colour=WHEN`
96	: When to use terminal colours (using ANSI escape code to colorize the output).
97	
98	Valid settings are ‘`always`’, ‘`automatic`’ (or ‘`auto`’ for short), and ‘`never`’.
99	When used without a value, defaults to ‘`automatic`’.
100	
101	The default behavior (‘`automatic`’ or ‘`auto`’) is to colorize the output only when the standard output is connected to a real terminal. If the output of `eza` is redirected to a file or piped into another program, terminal colors will not be used. Setting this option to ‘`always`’ causes `eza` to always output terminal color, while ‘`never`’ disables the use of terminal color.
102	
103	Manually setting this option overrides `NO_COLOR` environment.
104	
105	`--color-scale`, `--colour-scale`
106	: highlight levels of `field` distinctly.
107	Use comma(,) separated list of all, age, size
108	
109	`--color-scale-mode=MODE`, `--colour-scale-mode=MODE`
110	: Use gradient or fixed colors in `--color-scale`.
111	
112	Valid options are `fixed` or `gradient`.
113	When used without a value, defaults to `gradient`.
114	
115	`--icons=WHEN`
116	: Display icons next to file names.
117	
118	Valid settings are ‘`always`’, ‘`automatic`’ (‘`auto`’ for short), and ‘`never`’.
119	When used without a value, defaults to ‘`automatic`’.
120	
121	`automatic` or `auto` will display icons only when the standard output is connected to a real terminal. If `eza` is ran while in a `tty`, or the output of `eza` is either redirected to a file or piped into another program, icons will not be used. Setting this option to ‘`always`’ causes `eza` to always display icons, while ‘`never`’ disables the use of icons.
122	
123	`--no-quotes`
124	: Don't quote file names with spaces.
125	
126	`--hyperlink`
127	: Display entries as hyperlinks
128	
129	`-w`, `--width=COLS`
130	: Set screen width in columns.
